@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to. It throws an `Error`
+if the pointer is not valid (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be followed by `0` or
+`1`) or if it does not resolve to a value of the document: missing member, array index out of range
+or not in canonical form, the `-` token (which designates a nonexistent element), or a token applied
+to a scalar. Only own members of objects are followed, so `/__proto__` or `/toString` never resolve.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": [10, 20] }, "/a~1b/1"); // 20
+```
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
